  "captions": [
    {
      "text": "Imagine a powerful earthquake striking New",
      "start": 0.2,
      "end": 2.072
    },
    {
      "text": "York City.",
      "start": 2.072,
      "end": 2.6
    },
    {
      "text": "Buildings shaking.",
      "start": 2.64,
      "end": 3.757
    },
    {
      "text": "Streets cracking.",
      "start": 3.845,
      "end": 4.692
    },
    {
      "text": "Millions caught off guard.",
      "start": 4.764,
      "end": 5.907
    },
    {
      "text": "Sounds like Hollywood fiction?",
      "start": 5.947,
      "end": 7.184
    },
    {
      "text": "Think again.",
      "start": 7.484,
      "end": 8.141
    },
    {
      "text": "In eighteen eighty-four,",
      "start": 8.491,
      "end": 9.681
    },
    {
      "text": "an earthquake estimated at magnitude five",
      "start": 9.681,
      "end": 11.679
    },
    {
      "text": "point two shook New York.",
      "start": 11.679,
      "end": 13.245
    },
    {
      "text": "It damaged chimneys and brick buildings in",
      "start": 13.285,
      "end": 15.288
    },
    {
      "text": "New York and New Jersey.",
      "start": 15.288,
      "end": 16.444
    },
    {
      "text": "And in twenty twenty-four,",
      "start": 16.794,
      "end": 18.068
    },
    {
      "text": "a magnitude four point eight earthquake",
      "start": 18.068,
      "end": 20.036
    },
    {
      "text": "struck nearby New Jersey.",
      "start": 20.036,
      "end": 21.341
    },
    {
      "text": "Millions felt it.",
      "start": 21.381,
      "end": 22.274
    },
    {
      "text": "The USGS received more than one hundred",
      "start": 22.314,
      "end": 24.7
    },
    {
      "text": "eighty thousand reports,",
      "start": 24.7,
      "end": 25.996
    },
    {
      "text": "the most for any earthquake.",
      "start": 25.996,
      "end": 27.416
    },
    {
      "text": "But here’s what makes this truly unsettling.",
      "start": 27.766,
      "end": 30.005
    },
    {
      "text": "New York City’s official hazard plan cites",
      "start": 30.305,
      "end": 32.431
    },
    {
      "text": "USGS maps:",
      "start": 32.431,
      "end": 33.702
    },
    {
      "text": "a five to twenty-five percent chance of",
      "start": 33.742,
      "end": 35.965
    },
    {
      "text": "potentially damaging shaking in the next",
      "start": 35.965,
      "end": 37.965
    },
    {
      "text": "hundred years.",
      "start": 37.965,
      "end": 38.697
    },
    {
      "text": "And the biggest danger isn’t",
      "start": 38.997,
      "end": 40.163
    },
    {
      "text": "the skyscrapers.",
      "start": 40.163,
      "end": 40.99
    },
    {
      "text": "It’s older brick buildings,",
      "start": 41.03,
      "end": 42.362
    },
    {
      "text": "aging underground infrastructure,",
      "start": 42.362,
      "end": 43.924
    },
    {
      "text": "and soft ground.",
      "start": 43.924,
      "end": 44.92
    },
    {
      "text": "They could turn a moderate earthquake into",
      "start": 44.96,
      "end": 47.012
    },
    {
      "text": "a costly urban disaster.",
      "start": 47.012,
      "end": 48.445
    },
    {
      "text": "So, could a damaging earthquake hit",
      "start": 48.795,
      "end": 50.576
    },
    {
      "text": "New York?",
      "start": 50.576,
      "end": 51.051
    },
    {
      "text": "Yes.",
      "start": 51.134,
      "end": 51.552
    },
    {
      "text": "Is a catastrophic quake likely?",
      "start": 51.852,
      "end": 53.362
    },
    {
      "text": "No.",
      "start": 53.476,
      "end": 53.772
    },
    {
      "text": "Myth or fact?",
      "start": 54.072,
      "end": 54.982
    },
    {
      "text": "New York isn’t earthquake-proof.",
      "start": 55.064,
      "end": 56.449
    }
  ],
